From fbf7406f45c9bb601cdeb77d79a2eab43bd9b9f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: qualcomm-toolbox <169756160+qcom-toolbox@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 22:12:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] umi-0174-adreno-userclient-class-at-publish

IOServiceOpen on SweetAdreno failed with kIOReturnUnsupported: the
IOUserClientClass property was set in SweetAdreno::start(), but nothing
matches the service, so start() never runs and newUserClient finds no
class. Set it at publish time, as the other SWEET stand-ins
(IONetworkStack, IOAcceleratorES) do. Found with the verbose
sweet-gpu-test daemon over the file server (open -> 0xe00002c7 on every
retry, no kernel handleOpen line).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdreno.cpp | 4 ++++
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+)

diff --git a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdreno.cpp b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdreno.cpp
index 23f08a7..1420842 100644
--- a/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdreno.cpp
+++ b/iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAdreno.cpp
@@ -342,6 +342,10 @@ sweet_adreno_publish(IOService *provider)
 		return;
 	}
 	service->setName("SweetAdreno");
+	/* The user client class must be a property before anything opens the service:
+	 * nothing matches it, so start() never runs, and the open path (newUserClient)
+	 * reads this property to build the connection (as the other SWEET stand-ins do). */
+	service->setProperty(kIOUserClientClassKey, "SweetAdrenoUserClient");
 	if (service->attach(provider)) {
 		service->registerService();
 		IOLog("SWEET ADRENO: GPU service published (SweetAdreno; opens %s)\n",
-- 
